{"title":"Best Bikes, Bikepacking Gear & Tech at 2026 Outdoor Retailer","link":"https://bikerumor.com/best-bikes-gear-outdoor-retailer-2026/","date":1787419335000,"content":"<p><img src=\"/media/ffef9dee73720553ea7ff8c3e2bb7ff01f6cead9d40d359e2be3d2d69434b2eb.jpg\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" alt=\"donkey label titanium monster gravel bike.\" /></p>\n<p>While most of the crew is out west for the <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/interview-made-show-director-billy-sinkford-plus-a-discount-code-for-bikerumor-readers/\" target=\"_blank\">MADE Bike Show</a>, I rolled through <a href=\"https://www.outdoorretailer.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Outdoor Retailer’s</a> new venue in Minneapolis, MN, to see what’s new for other outdoor activities. Turns out, there was quite a bit of very cool bike stuff on display, plus some camping gear that was perfectly suited for bikepacking, and more! Here’s the best cycling bits from OR2026…</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Donkey Label Titanium Gravel Bike</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/42593280a7195fd426210f3cba4a6d94145dd100006a9006240511921d5041a5.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/42593280a7195fd426210f3cba4a6d94145dd100006a9006240511921d5041a5.jpg\" alt=\"headtube and badge closeup on donkey label titanium monster gravel bike.\" srcset=\"/media/42593280a7195fd426210f3cba4a6d94145dd100006a9006240511921d5041a5.jpg 2000w, /media/8e6d0c3f6f29663dee87a5e2e2bc80fb7fc2908dec931de45c81816b12ca0097.jpg 297w, /media/5ae6deea64375e8ca42241697b68c6e228c96a0fd3e0e4679f13678b440aa38d.jpg 1536w, /media/50706f93180319b1c75e0a2e77fca83881f3f9d6a18a172093a01eb6a198f760.jpg 120w, /media/3b5433d6207f759fe733731ba9404f085c04d0e6fbc805501d4887aee22fe86d.jpg 768w, /media/dca71b8de53d4c5e004c6acf5db21f9e43dcb9775b3ef08aa3503b0cc2ea20ea.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>While they weren’t using the word, I’ll say it – Monster Gravel. This beast crammed 29×2.35″ mountain bike tires into the frame and fork. Realistically, it’s designed for up to 700×50, as tires this big create some real clearance issues, particularly at the fork’s crown. And they raise the BB height, and your center of gravity, which takes the handling down a notch.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"/media/d69369b1af5ab2d7dcc8ee522430b0edb1f74a7b7f362b6ddad7e76ed5c45b86.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" src=\"/media/db3c0c5aeefbc2471ec2d890486d42291710c4198d9284bdcf8b727efc007c8b.jpg\" alt=\"tire clearance closeup on donkey label titanium monster gravel bike.\" srcset=\"/media/db3c0c5aeefbc2471ec2d890486d42291710c4198d9284bdcf8b727efc007c8b.jpg 1536w, /media/dc7a2de4eedcb143df9178f02cc03d691266f6958c9427c13ea531cbddb9e199.jpg 297w, /media/fa8b37b5cdb1a04102ea1a071e40dffbce61dc0d3f3aff0cf6f9fa84d5bedcaf.jpg 120w, /media/897e963ff420ffb74eec5b1f0e05f885a8838bbfc03f5f4b05c915d137c190b4.jpg 768w, /media/1e9db977010637653e6554294798f5f17e5f943d7ad882a0b83b73ceca0f4772.jpg 1200w, /media/d69369b1af5ab2d7dcc8ee522430b0edb1f74a7b7f362b6ddad7e76ed5c45b86.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/ff7952ca407e3bf5308ea74fdd3d7161d31528a12af981941a0515ff4eda82fd.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" src=\"/media/0e603c011b30c0ea61849db8c2b297b4b287cfffd9bf0a930acf632483b6d363.jpg\" alt=\"chainstay yoke closeup on donkey label titanium monster gravel bike.\" srcset=\"/media/0e603c011b30c0ea61849db8c2b297b4b287cfffd9bf0a930acf632483b6d363.jpg 1536w, /media/4b02732af6f7814f020a1e949e6bec637b3331a088d1222b7efeb65f6b066f3c.jpg 297w, /media/d1900fcc424c2db911a2250eee6da02dbed9f708885199d4d761b810ef64985b.jpg 120w, /media/c146bb1f2821b2cf2f60c3812596e883d1ae5dcec1d5fd76a70ff1396881d13b.jpg 768w, /media/07806b194bb1ce754d572e6ea3945f84f1dfbe21803f503ccbed8f891767e683.jpg 1200w, /media/ff7952ca407e3bf5308ea74fdd3d7161d31528a12af981941a0515ff4eda82fd.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/2c9581374599f20a75cbfda80bac7c9347a2f2763b4e8331b88506f424c5deb2.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" src=\"/media/f75cb3007175762d1d60ef0b56cccef0012590c8e13d08f5cf345e259033ca4b.jpg\" alt=\"chainstay yoke closeup on donkey label titanium monster gravel bike.\" srcset=\"/media/f75cb3007175762d1d60ef0b56cccef0012590c8e13d08f5cf345e259033ca4b.jpg 1536w, /media/8cc0ab5a843877368e83e52619f4b07e2731034b687eae78b147e50013af095e.jpg 297w, /media/91a3aa32f4f6e4d5132b4c94da444059d348850aba93355d6e8c53f1b3a1a2b9.jpg 120w, /media/1993819d7b3db5edf1e25f94ba7a560e531a4959c33ff64deb7f5a41c5a939ee.jpg 768w, /media/bda69b97221d3740875100e01f84b6e4dc479932d3ef49bbe3beb9f948bb6b96.jpg 1200w, /media/2c9581374599f20a75cbfda80bac7c9347a2f2763b4e8331b88506f424c5deb2.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Regardless, they had two prototypes on display, one polished and this brushed one, both titanium and both looking very near ready for production.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"/media/ae0a05b9b714538676834ee5c3c495b5d27812164c42da6373578087d6961e18.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" src=\"/media/ed319ab96412d680e661c880643dd20a160c0f4cbf7b0592c50fa4e23ff75d54.jpg\" alt=\"dropouts closeup on donkey label titanium monster gravel bike.\" srcset=\"/media/ed319ab96412d680e661c880643dd20a160c0f4cbf7b0592c50fa4e23ff75d54.jpg 1536w, /media/6f096d59300dd2271f2b75835a2a2818e6c34ed61cb8399080c69cbdfeb2b21d.jpg 297w, /media/4b437b67238db8946e921030003d8403fb05abf9b67341c9e6491768aac87591.jpg 120w, /media/f6c567c8a9fe6756c4239724ac2f137155f53971141b7edeb4ca4af26a06a307.jpg 768w, /media/3097e50c8c12f6464779ff5efecdc98b722b133060695cce5458bd28b89718b8.jpg 1200w, /media/ae0a05b9b714538676834ee5c3c495b5d27812164c42da6373578087d6961e18.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/c83662550960888f7c6181d48aa350d997a7eefdc970b61d7052452b071cf5a2.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" src=\"/media/ae5fbcae313b6f6f077a57b2bbcf24847010a4c72f1fc7c82edc3c360bbe3088.jpg\" alt=\"seatpost closeup on donkey label titanium monster gravel bike.\" srcset=\"/media/ae5fbcae313b6f6f077a57b2bbcf24847010a4c72f1fc7c82edc3c360bbe3088.jpg 1536w, /media/64259acd355c4ebffb092fb8f6006396f3f8713877c90a3813f453ad4aefcd9f.jpg 297w, /media/02b8a61b9c94d34b6b19000bbeb23d57c8be24d568982964e4abb0aa71c2dc07.jpg 120w, /media/68c595ca5b9a660f57f91708aa42e0bf5a888ba7c0963fabfd99ccb45845cc23.jpg 768w, /media/bf1a63a0fc52dffd7d9312a33b8a409e0600ed2e8db399aec901eb48f68c2e99.jpg 1200w, /media/c83662550960888f7c6181d48aa350d997a7eefdc970b61d7052452b071cf5a2.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/a60ec19a006a3cac86d481ff671f52cc58d449d4a8388cf692e031623421f81e.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" src=\"/media/5c123e29a1187b60ea55f9afff223e4fea3ccb0055a023c107faebada6fd2050.jpg\" alt=\"dropout closeup on donkey label titanium monster gravel bike.\" srcset=\"/media/5c123e29a1187b60ea55f9afff223e4fea3ccb0055a023c107faebada6fd2050.jpg 1536w, /media/3afe75be90e64fbe20822d2a4677b325e39a08b632090dde973040e1f7c40581.jpg 297w, /media/e222fc4c1e94f44971041139e6dbf1460be5727f577dc49fae867fc10cd1ab58.jpg 120w, /media/dc2f051ff8d5bead9f05af46ce6a5a8cead86732686dff85d11282d6ec5e8546.jpg 768w, /media/e4e80c1c39a222be3e2ef76fad0554572d8da8f4657c26ad754e03ba2e895822.jpg 1200w, /media/a60ec19a006a3cac86d481ff671f52cc58d449d4a8388cf692e031623421f81e.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>No word on pricing or availability yet. If you’re wondering who <a href=\"https://donkeylabel.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Donkey Label</a> is, they’re better known for their cycling clothing, which is pretty cool. But they partnered with an MPLS design firm and, together, they wanted to make a bike. I’d say it looks pretty good for a first effort!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Wolf Tooth, Otso, Cedaero, Surly &amp; Wilde</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/4a515ac6976dc640b680a66998d9671b0071c2749daafe089aba3807d289398c.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/4a515ac6976dc640b680a66998d9671b0071c2749daafe089aba3807d289398c.jpg\" alt=\"wolf tooth components and Otso bikes with color-matched Cedaero bike bags.\" srcset=\"/media/4a515ac6976dc640b680a66998d9671b0071c2749daafe089aba3807d289398c.jpg 2000w, /media/3586599d40a6ee186e2f55a702d65306c54bdf8ae3dd822e2704347a724978c7.jpg 297w, /media/3d19880f433f691a44252ba069de2b00010a853836270a983eed9094b0b33ccf.jpg 1536w, /media/717dce52a618cbd64445c12b8afbc5f9ac4055d34cc65931079b162d9ec5812f.jpg 120w, /media/e1df3839a6245c44c5cd2d1caaa7c259c70e38d1b9c01bd601d5b91721163484.jpg 768w, /media/c7e8c99ea7890fdae782d875ae707f51172f7fce9cdf55155b2be1acfe9ac3f7.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>While we’re on bikes, several other area brands had displays. While not new, this <a href=\"https://otsocycles.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Otso</a> was decked out with sister-brand <a href=\"https://www.wolftoothcomponents.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Wolf Tooth Components</a>‘ gold-anodized bits…</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/fb3ad7cb8788fee5df599e105837291029be9f7f26e629defb695e5ef7e90816.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/fb3ad7cb8788fee5df599e105837291029be9f7f26e629defb695e5ef7e90816.jpg\" alt=\"wolf tooth components and Otso bikes with color-matched Cedaero bike bags.\" srcset=\"/media/fb3ad7cb8788fee5df599e105837291029be9f7f26e629defb695e5ef7e90816.jpg 2000w, /media/a1b93f64f8c8c51b735d3ab1a0baf8916fabf7b49ae6b9ab1e3578f7441d1d70.jpg 297w, /media/3a9eaa5241faebf3e84010c427bcec6549273d28bc3413a9ec7e60385f7bf142.jpg 1536w, /media/cc41858f00f4227fd85db43151e05bcc36856c8db08cfc34b12cb9f0d44f6b3a.jpg 120w, /media/648636b2980c412dd31ecf23a5efc07327747034fdd5651cb2b31788b85c3e0f.jpg 768w, /media/a6b6cf8a2f6cb8644c7531c7c5b257a06e44a730fde89db1c6907ff5abbcee76.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>…which were color-matched perfectly by <a href=\"https://cedaero.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Cedaero</a> for their handlebar and seat bags.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/0f21846d3c9a37619bbd6d00dc8a28b493ed99a4c9894b05e91d946dfe2c1732.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/0f21846d3c9a37619bbd6d00dc8a28b493ed99a4c9894b05e91d946dfe2c1732.jpg\" alt=\"surly moonlander fat bike at outdoor retailer 2026 show.\" srcset=\"/media/0f21846d3c9a37619bbd6d00dc8a28b493ed99a4c9894b05e91d946dfe2c1732.jpg 2000w, /media/a46220d920c1104c53952f9f133011d2f404b7dfe929afd2a1df9f423a210dbd.jpg 297w, /media/bebe5ae4f70e5342bd8b09f8e29c05d8bfcf1e6ff61be8eb1f03e6f8f02b714c.jpg 1536w, /media/39a2b89d174d5a4a60337fb06da6e993a35ea433cc81a698a791ea434de34701.jpg 120w, /media/92d6009d6ace667c832555b4a0f305009958db155f79cb0cba08835df0fdb326.jpg 768w, /media/1c27a83b82e9194e98eb0d2419230062e9af60805fafb37d85ecb1a42437f46a.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The Surly Moonlander was built around gargantuan 24×6.2″ tires. Yes, that’s <em>SIX</em>-point-two inch wide tires. Throw in a long wheelbase and low standover and it’s a bike designed for riding places most people wouldn’t consider. Read <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/surly-moonlander-takes-off-with-24-x-6-2-tires-and-pinion-gearbox/\">all about it here</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/2c34cb2c8f8949e01010bec02b7e983258b6d2551b5383457a5a04b34a3ce30a.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/2c34cb2c8f8949e01010bec02b7e983258b6d2551b5383457a5a04b34a3ce30a.jpg\" alt=\"wilde bikes at outdoor retailer 2026.\" srcset=\"/media/2c34cb2c8f8949e01010bec02b7e983258b6d2551b5383457a5a04b34a3ce30a.jpg 2000w, /media/c9de5de7c9d047126417377731bfb2f0fee95d3a80a5e40070a59321c57d65f7.jpg 297w, /media/9eb9ac2ea95b31a2914b7008be56b2beaad1b367b21e223bedd66b4e3f0c8fa6.jpg 1536w, /media/fd7ce98ef0b2c527ec9528bea3b33a7be6148996324ea1047dda9584984b7082.jpg 120w, /media/556da666af21c72408eb62162dc79d103ba770f4818306eb4ba9b3688fe006d8.jpg 768w, /media/259b3e0e005f23ad3410871a55ef2f22d13fed7109e885868f715f1b62ed6072.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Wilde is <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/?s=wilde\">a brand that gets it</a> – bikes should be fun, and their designs and pricing prove it. Sure, they’ve got titanium models, too, but their steel 26″ clunker comes in under $2k complete.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Bikepacking: Hyperlite, Trailbrush, Dry Brew &amp; Buzz Bomb</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/917769fb35a0023b4f08b702d83a73ff37c961a9c366688d6253dafbc248ca1c.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/917769fb35a0023b4f08b702d83a73ff37c961a9c366688d6253dafbc248ca1c.jpg\" alt=\"hyperlite bikepacking tent.\" srcset=\"/media/917769fb35a0023b4f08b702d83a73ff37c961a9c366688d6253dafbc248ca1c.jpg 2000w, /media/bf6ae8d68c267984a65040e9c05c6d4888c0d8a0468664e6e8b88cc59b97b432.jpg 297w, /media/c6aceb2fe6cc219223e7664d0ee52542b2c34a3c1929526d0d67817708468bb1.jpg 1536w, /media/d9a4af20a91e9ddc2e385d4a5be0dfc590d7421cb7530d841ed62c6debb0b851.jpg 120w, /media/ab3e472ddc0f3f08326bc0ec8d6b48e97ea669083d0a5da75f8d7d5ec9ecc1b3.jpg 768w, /media/b6d74bc54954ee6d3de7d09b9583bf92b74e59f352c2e58439aee3118c687ccf.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Hyperlite, as the name suggests, makes ridiculously lightweight camping gear. This <a href=\"https://hyperlitemountaingear.com/products/crosspeak-1\" target=\"_blank\">CrossPeak 1</a> tent weighs just 28.7oz (813.6g) all in. The shell and floor are 100% waterproof Dyneema, and there’s a generous vestibule once the guy-lines are run to pop out the rainfly shell, perfect for keeping your helmet, bags, etc., protected from the elements (or just hidden from view).</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/491ec1ac9fa13b3403a776af3a0cd3602b75e711001e113b2b65d8c5393f39f4.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/491ec1ac9fa13b3403a776af3a0cd3602b75e711001e113b2b65d8c5393f39f4.jpg\" alt=\"top view of hyperlite bikepacking tent.\" srcset=\"/media/491ec1ac9fa13b3403a776af3a0cd3602b75e711001e113b2b65d8c5393f39f4.jpg 2000w, /media/5a6b795542954763570a820b09241a90dfdf6d5867a53d964ec87f110f42509d.jpg 297w, /media/5ebd507aba5974e6e89a82a4291e70ccf34d20a1369cc2612e025c04582ec466.jpg 1536w, /media/515a5151e269bf4906db2e28ae680b8d653e27875aff9251f756f08c81c622b6.jpg 120w, /media/410f738dc2907bacc0a1652263fca04a15ee1ae41a8de9d8e8a461eee6ae5434.jpg 768w, /media/4f6f8892c0f050fa6df91cfbed4d6f3493102e33f71ac6cffcf68575d14d8a81.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>While it’s not specifically made for bikepacking, they say the pole segments are pretty short for the main (gray) frame poles. The cross bar orange) that creates width at the top has the longest segment, around 15.5″. As long as you have a packing solution for that part, it’s among the lightest solo tents on the market. They make a two-person version, also.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/7bd0239dea3894aab1fb3635a950d919000f69925a2084f4518d309c8610f5d4.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/7bd0239dea3894aab1fb3635a950d919000f69925a2084f4518d309c8610f5d4.jpg\" alt=\"trailbrush ultralight toothbrush clipped to a spoon.\" srcset=\"/media/7bd0239dea3894aab1fb3635a950d919000f69925a2084f4518d309c8610f5d4.jpg 2000w, /media/4deebadfdb4295ce5ac714bb592b09bfb149e52802bdcf6cef40467380c1183e.jpg 297w, /media/8b65be5f8bee375f49348901b520885f87e322f4324190aded8ceed7a184fa2b.jpg 1536w, /media/782146b9c69eaa4ac2b8b38874c82bf7896fd8f953ad9a3890e049acda55824b.jpg 120w, /media/5977ba24aebcaa22fa2fa49ed1441110bdfb883b5982b1bf487da2854819805f.jpg 768w, /media/97d1ecbc624e43cbe7eedb3128767c4ecb8bccc4bab2872a8dbfbd91be2ce4e6.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The <a href=\"https://trailbrush.com/products/trailbrush\" target=\"_blank\">Trailbrush</a> was the ultimate weight-weenie item at the show. It turns most camp utensils into a toothbrush, weighs less than a penny, and is purposefully designed for camping. How? The bristles are fewer, with wider spacing between bunches, so you don’t need as much water to rinse it clean.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The brush head slots into a small hole found on most camp spoons, turning the spoon into the handle. That gives you a proper length handle compared to cutting down a regular toothbrush, and also means a lot less plastic being used for something you’re just going to cut down and throw away anyway.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/e39037fc29d57d9e837ad736b00f4765acc2397b432cc0ec76f52afedf4ac57a.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/e39037fc29d57d9e837ad736b00f4765acc2397b432cc0ec76f52afedf4ac57a.jpg\" alt=\"dry brew chewable coffee snacks.\" srcset=\"/media/e39037fc29d57d9e837ad736b00f4765acc2397b432cc0ec76f52afedf4ac57a.jpg 2000w, /media/4ae4b0671f6c96cb91cef199dc5aa62f7d134c4af189f20b3a1dffbd8c8de472.jpg 297w, /media/911c790ce8881eb1e49fe223d3f6937de37ea96e573e8a4113a38a34b7bf0924.jpg 1536w, /media/79a2cf14f27f9ebc5c60eced51ba7c71cf5e77f27936272495194b65c2a28897.jpg 120w, /media/9c3c941473529cfde2ab31ba5f681c95dc16536de281b02410f23b02e230933c.jpg 768w, /media/d5a18f5301a2997a8426440fc99be40edf7d3a943965bf66bb40b44bbd2f5f28.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>If you’ve cut out the camp stove and extra water to save weight, too, <a href=\"https://drybrew.com/?srsltid=AfmBOopoeYxJLOgDinnSbScFnmg8Gw-TTwcl-fHjuMTMFjeQ7z2HQhfh\" target=\"_blank\">Dry Brew</a> makes coffee into a Tootsie Roll-like snack. The single serve packets have about a cup’s worth of coffee each, and tins and bigger bags let you dose it how you wish.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/6362f5d4f039a29f1e24021a0942cd6bf2f71a429f3a5f2a9a5a182336681876.jpg\"><img width=\"1800\" height=\"1350\" src=\"/media/6362f5d4f039a29f1e24021a0942cd6bf2f71a429f3a5f2a9a5a182336681876.jpg\" alt=\"buzz bomb powdered caffeine packets.\" srcset=\"/media/6362f5d4f039a29f1e24021a0942cd6bf2f71a429f3a5f2a9a5a182336681876.jpg 1800w, /media/e54e32b6391c7f60a8fb1c3deadc18437ab8118ac1d7d5be9cd7f0fd7b1bdbb2.jpg 297w, /media/0976d2a84088a993ed0b0bdef9997f2b99fef2a4610435a976d1915b4872c2e2.jpg 1536w, /media/dc106f345b4f94de4c66e2eef113031bf41047c91c211621bad255b30596d536.jpg 120w, /media/a55e75543873d92e2021d88e9b7564a29c9ebc9764ef9154e3312fb053af24f4.jpg 768w, /media/3571f1eeaef69edeef7178c103b1fc74d8d4cca78d1d47aeb6de8894d8e2f995.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>And if those are too much weight, <a href=\"https://buzzbombcaffeine.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Buzz Bomb</a> is flavored caffeine powder that you dissolve under your tongue for an instant boost. No wasted time or effort chewing, guzzling, or even digesting.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Other Cool Stuff</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/0db0b0b6c91c069c3edda19be111e71a5e3a39fe96062448a042d7bf9b50078e.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/0db0b0b6c91c069c3edda19be111e71a5e3a39fe96062448a042d7bf9b50078e.jpg\" alt=\"kopilot RFID id tag for athletes on a bicycle helmet.\" srcset=\"/media/0db0b0b6c91c069c3edda19be111e71a5e3a39fe96062448a042d7bf9b50078e.jpg 2000w, /media/875284d4aa8bacafb62b0bcfb1c60cb8c08d230f92c8703b3ef23fb25d2be571.jpg 297w, /media/01c4e069d9262bb78d1b29661185d3250b2fa150d4de06bb99a8ca25ceb55c8e.jpg 1536w, /media/a8d9ee0bf81639e70278ea421e3693c7689912b3e95fd5576ba2809b5174275d.jpg 120w, /media/3603b0d22cdbc2f3b0ac583e65aa41c4f65449ac37a7b012c1e66f2c8bd2f9d5.jpg 768w, /media/71d2d2770ed761c7f00ee0b25c1be552db13824942e606c05d5b2b7c42978544.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Introduced last fall, <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/kopilot-id-nfc-emergency-helmet-google-tag/\" target=\"_blank\">Kopilot.ID</a> is a simple RFID tag that you stick to your helmet, then create your free account. There’s no battery, no subscription, and nothing else to do. Just input your personal, medical &amp; emergency contact info, then anyone can hold their NFC-equipped phone (which is most modern phones) near the tag to see your emergency medical info if you’re unresponsive.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/ed5fce4c6bb7c8535f93968ebab93775fafc340d3e8ff7a02e7e9afda1bd5433.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1340\" src=\"/media/ed5fce4c6bb7c8535f93968ebab93775fafc340d3e8ff7a02e7e9afda1bd5433.jpg\" alt=\"for the black bicycle helmets for african american hairstyles.\" srcset=\"/media/ed5fce4c6bb7c8535f93968ebab93775fafc340d3e8ff7a02e7e9afda1bd5433.jpg 2000w, /media/7e830b6132dff722a44ffc9597870b7453ee045ec04c454a7632359f149f883e.jpg 297w, /media/87872a1f9fd37d732457baf864868c5910cc8a7e5f208a5bb304fb0a70bb798d.jpg 1536w, /media/5e47ffb2bf3db01dc3c76ddb7ff7f8dd156b2c2ceb22a458adbf757e37ed5913.jpg 120w, /media/231d19d9f2dd5b1293f5d60770d59c825f5263e804a3d91c410db9f15b467a97.jpg 768w, /media/a0af9966bcc83d3af14160dfc5b70c2c5f534db56733f5945803e39282d18f69.jpg 1343w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>4theBLK Helmets, by <a href=\"https://www.bicipr3ta.com/\" target=\"_blank\">BiciPr3ta</a>, is, according to Google, a “Brazilian socio-environmental enterprise based in Salvador, Bahia, focused on Black cycling mobility. Founded by creative entrepreneur Lívia Suarez, the brand creates products, projects, and cultural initiatives—most notably designing and producing Helmets 4theBLK, the country’s first line of urban bicycle helmets specifically adapted for afro hair, braids, and dreadlocks.”</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/1ff314c74158c3a6a5bc7f25820c52e1d70148feab25cc03455e80040c300fa1.jpg\"><img width=\"1800\" height=\"1350\" src=\"/media/1ff314c74158c3a6a5bc7f25820c52e1d70148feab25cc03455e80040c300fa1.jpg\" alt=\"for the black bicycle helmets for african american hairstyles.\" srcset=\"/media/1ff314c74158c3a6a5bc7f25820c52e1d70148feab25cc03455e80040c300fa1.jpg 1800w, /media/d243cc2d718eb8eefac1d41013a5dc89ce219a1eda6cf317bad4fc07b48b3da9.jpg 297w, /media/a4f59c45f3b6ec77adb8bf988e00e9d1fef7b1c96383e280062326a15e5f020c.jpg 1536w, /media/d24e9b6b6eb156d6cc2887e76b84885959f2db6480d61a3ce4c1422c8f9c638c.jpg 120w, /media/ea9c7ee1b82daf167476d350d57152222fb830cd49f1de5da04b20f6f807437f.jpg 768w, /media/b7502a0cfa484a445cbe3286dffdad7b727f7332dee32ceb144c42a2916ced96.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The shell is thin, with lightweight foam padding inside. It’s made for casual, low-speed cycling around town, not mountain biking or faster road/gravel cycling.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/c9f38650f95384263eba6577df582e7a9789f92171f33387a153589db11ed23e.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/c9f38650f95384263eba6577df582e7a9789f92171f33387a153589db11ed23e.jpg\" alt=\"formula 100 bicycle care product lineup.\" srcset=\"/media/c9f38650f95384263eba6577df582e7a9789f92171f33387a153589db11ed23e.jpg 2000w, /media/23b60b03ec191b547e0ef5cd94aaa71f974bc9a53a91b22550096716209a6b5d.jpg 297w, /media/405e06f25d90b6571579d99307ca728d6251f25cf26c02d71cb319d931b4ddcc.jpg 1536w, /media/50e153c37f10f429431e2393ee4c3a20c4303b221422b8e8a6d7c5580489ee95.jpg 120w, /media/6fa0b1e18a76bf9a3b7bb4c017fc63cf4a4fb2fe4b6c7655be608fd50d5e98cd.jpg 768w, /media/22dfc1726ff337ed9b419009e4788ac1aacb4f018069d885c7b7981de9aec08a.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https://formula100.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Formula 100</a> is a German brand of bicycle care, and when I asked what makes them better/special/different, the reply was genius – “We use science.” Check out the full line on their website, but two things that stood out at OR were the Bike Wash and chain brush.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/1bdf50e35593b437b7ddad35b6466ece5146e18ea41e5dfd8ee5a4f02a8d77a4.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/1bdf50e35593b437b7ddad35b6466ece5146e18ea41e5dfd8ee5a4f02a8d77a4.jpg\" alt=\"formula 100 gel bike wash spray.\" srcset=\"/media/1bdf50e35593b437b7ddad35b6466ece5146e18ea41e5dfd8ee5a4f02a8d77a4.jpg 2000w, /media/680b51ce22f49b6da11311de400c325894a385c10ebe6654975c5d072e77a6de.jpg 297w, /media/8b5b670785caeefc47010c7d515404bf4f9389d95850f3c96e5220580c31849d.jpg 1536w, /media/4b0e8a6c1f527db8f96e51f6c854c3f4a3afe98473abad84e1a533736621f169.jpg 120w, /media/5cb0f26a20c578d0625130a5f88d521b9d005b7628bff54e8335927900810aaa.jpg 768w, /media/b9a811195418c4c22069f12f565781a2bdcc42b2da8353fe2d352cccb4aa5102.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The Express Wash is a rinse-free solution, just spray on and wipe off. More interesting is the Clean Machine, a gel-based spray that goes on thick and won’t run:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/e975113c3f825ba8aad2d95b0a609bee90a4163cae53b13ac4638739d53ec8e3.jpg\"><img width=\"2025\" height=\"1000\" src=\"/media/e975113c3f825ba8aad2d95b0a609bee90a4163cae53b13ac4638739d53ec8e3.jpg\" alt=\"formula 100 gel bike wash spray.\" srcset=\"/media/e975113c3f825ba8aad2d95b0a609bee90a4163cae53b13ac4638739d53ec8e3.jpg 2025w, /media/d464c6a55340e6091a6bd1b4ae67f191612489a03936eaa80ce47d78e19bd64d.jpg 297w, /media/86035b2f7ba12450e91b27e5189b6179d88fd6cd082b267bb4fa18150088ebb9.jpg 1536w, /media/6a1e33d69e9d5a1d20453fd80da2c5a09be1ac1a2dfaa3163b9eea4a94f77c21.jpg 120w, /media/92a43f01e6f337ae733f9907fb05bf69b19d442b33486d9ae94707fcc75b729a.jpg 768w, /media/3cb9a332310db009469b1b445c3cd51e180099a5094d97d2475c08339b3c1f94.jpg 1600w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>As long as your aim is true, it’ll it on the bike and dissolve grime and gunk, making it easier to scrub or wipe off, then rinse it clean. It does this without hurting the paint, finish, seals, or anything else. In fact, both are designed to use on any part of your bike, including drivetrain and brakes.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/11c763bd3e93e1b3b7410bbce9c0bf24860f4f42fd4957f0e5c0ed631d7de5db.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/11c763bd3e93e1b3b7410bbce9c0bf24860f4f42fd4957f0e5c0ed631d7de5db.jpg\" alt=\"formula 100 bicycle chain cleaning brush.\" srcset=\"/media/11c763bd3e93e1b3b7410bbce9c0bf24860f4f42fd4957f0e5c0ed631d7de5db.jpg 2000w, /media/f5fa1b1e62180c9f305757087ad20d808dbb1c507f9fb0974ba62045321a3dc3.jpg 297w, /media/edd7ac770f0f54d9fcf5f66532654b0d17ffe0664041fc0c657bdcb7c43a40d7.jpg 1536w, /media/94985519d11262020b24af59c064c52ccd68a1f22ef3443c02441c6d03d781c1.jpg 120w, /media/0967319bcc4c0aa1563e2f303e1d2c59acb43ad7cac2ee13028fb257d9661eb4.jpg 768w, /media/0513e1287883bfe82f61a43230200ee35f608bec282aa03c7919e8d6c420cadf.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>I also really liked their chain brush because it’s the only one I’ve seen with bristles to hit all four sides of the chain. Most only have three, so I have to flip it over, but this does the whole chain at once. Brilliant.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"/media/ee5549ae5988b7a405218ea0a03ccfd5beb3aab61690a5c8c29425e9a80fd604.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"/media/ee5549ae5988b7a405218ea0a03ccfd5beb3aab61690a5c8c29425e9a80fd604.jpg\" alt=\"drye fan bladder dryer for camelbak and hhydrapak reservoirs.\" srcset=\"/media/ee5549ae5988b7a405218ea0a03ccfd5beb3aab61690a5c8c29425e9a80fd604.jpg 2000w, /media/5fce02f11f98ad54fbcfef3195b2f586b2ce7f1802a86e76e2cea24909192354.jpg 297w, /media/3bd5a2831d0a3545288700174fc0dca171b66aeed4827a5ac5fe7e8ef8d8e7c0.jpg 1536w, /media/beaa6e63bd543ba8788285bb336b61f9fa2d6a93648aa501e363874c1913f8b6.jpg 120w, /media/a561f6b4cbb9be5e9b32bba8972d8f99a231b3a316958f02f805bb1389c1b694.jpg 768w, /media/c05dbdde0afbe9066586e56dbccf04a489d776801e4b12d96f7df59bf2c75c53.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The <a href=\"https://dryefan.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Drye Fan</a> is a rechargeable, compact fan that attaches directly to your Camelbak reservoir. Turn it on, choose one of three fan speeds, then decide how long you want it to run for (each light = one hour), then come back to a clean, dry bladder.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>They crushed its Kickstarter campaign <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/the-drye-fan-aims-to-make-cleaning-hydration-pack-reservoirs-a-breeze/\">last year</a>, and they’ll soon have attachments to work with bladders from Nathan and Hydrapak, too. Kits include the mounting adapter and a hanging hook that clips into the hose port.</p>","author":"Tyler Benedict","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/best-bikes-gear-outdoor-retailer-2026/#respond","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"51ab2f8b6b4c23167f6d9c344855dfa7e38d0fb9991a8d2efdbba9626fc23d8a","category":"Cycling"}